{"spec_element": "invariant", "proof_obligation": "preservation", "diagnosis": "The loop invariant 'forall k :: 0 <= k < (i) - 1 ==> result[k] == Power(l[k], n)' uses i-1 as the upper bound instead of i. After appending result[i] and incrementing i, the new invariant requires coverage up to k < i, but the old invariant only covered k < i-1, leaving element at position i-1 unaccounted for. This breaks preservation and also prevents deriving the postcondition after the loop."}
EOF

